+++ b/docs/superpowers/specs/2026-06-24-issue-156-development-pr-links-design.md
@@ -0,0 +1,187 @@
+# Issue Development PR Links Design
+
+Issue: #156 - when the agent takes and completes an issue make sure to link the PR back to the issue through the development section, and let users link PRs there.
+
+Date: 2026-06-24.
+
+## Context
+
+ForkMesh issues live in `issues/<number>/` with signed append-only markdown events.
+ForkMesh pull requests live in `pulls/<number>/` with signed PR metadata and signed conversation events.
+The Qt client already has an issue sidebar with a `Development` section.
+The Qt client already has a PR header action for linking an issue.
+Manual linking currently works by posting reciprocal thread comments.
+An issue-side note says `Linked pull request #N.`
+A PR-side note says `Linked issue #N.`
+The current issue sidebar discovers linked PRs by scanning PR references and issue-thread link notes.
+Agent-created PRs currently store `AgentSession::prNumber` and include issue text in the PR description.
+
+## Problem
+
+Issue #156 needs the agent-completion path and the user-driven link path to behave like one feature.
+The current baseline mostly infers agent-created PR links from session state and PR text.
+That makes the link visible only while local agent session metadata is present and refreshed.
+It also means the issue thread may not get an explicit durable note that the PR was linked.
+Manual linking is present, but the parsing and link-detection behavior sits inside `MainWindow`, which makes it harder to test directly.
+The issue detail pane may also need an explicit refresh after an agent creates a PR so the `Development` section updates immediately.
+
+## Decision
+
+Keep the existing issue sidebar `Development` section and reciprocal comment model.
+Make agent-created PRs use the same durable link note model as manual links.
+When an agent successfully creates a PR for an issue, ForkMesh should add `Linked pull request #N.` to the issue thread and `Linked issue #M.` to the PR thread.
+The PR description should continue to include the issue reference because it is useful context and helps mirrors that have not yet received issue comments.
+Move the reference extraction rules into a small helper so manual links, agent links, close-on-merge, and tests can share the same behavior.
+Refresh the open PR list and the currently selected issue detail after the agent PR is created.
+
+## Goals
+
+Show agent-created PRs in the issue sidebar `Development` section immediately after the agent completes.
+Persist the link in issue and PR history, not only in local `AgentSession` metadata.
+Let users link a PR from the issue sidebar.
+Let users link an issue from the PR header.
+Avoid duplicate link comments when the same issue and PR are already linked.
+Keep existing `closes #N`, `fixes #N`, `issue #N`, and explicit `Linked issue #N` behavior working.
+Add focused tests for link extraction and agent-created PR link persistence.
+
+## Non-Goals
+
+Do not add a new issue event type for development links in this issue.
+Do not rewrite existing issue or PR history.
+Do not change the signed issue or PR canonical formats.
+Do not require relay or Worker schema changes.
+Do not automatically merge or close PRs.
+Do not replace the existing manual link buttons with a larger relationship editor.
+
+## User Experience
+
+The issue sidebar keeps the current `Development` heading.
+When no PR is linked, it should show `No linked pull requests.`
+When PRs are linked, it should list each as a clickable `pull request #N`.
+The existing pull-request icon button next to `Development` remains the entry point for manual linking from the issue page.
+The PR header keeps its `Link issue` action.
+After a user links an issue and PR, both threads get visible comments that explain the relationship.
+After an agent creates a PR from an issue, the same visible relationship appears without a second manual action.
+If the user is already viewing the issue when the agent completes, the Development section should update in place.
+
+## Link Model
+
+The first implementation should keep links as ordinary signed comments.
+This is compatible with the current append-only store and relay inbox.
+It also makes links visible to users who inspect issue and PR conversations outside the sidebar.
+
+The durable issue-side comment should be:
+
+```text
+Linked pull request #<prNumber>.
+```
+
+The durable PR-side comment should be:
+
+```text
+Linked issue #<issueNumber>.
+```
+
+Before writing either comment, the UI should check whether the relationship is already discoverable.
+If the relationship already exists, the UI should not add duplicate link notes.
+
+## Reference Extraction
+
+Create a small helper for extracting issue numbers from PR text and PR numbers from issue text.
+The helper should cover existing behavior:
+
+- `issue #123`
+- `issue-123`
+- `closes #123`
+- `closed #123`
+- `fixes #123`
+- `fixed #123`
+- `resolves #123`
+- `resolved #123`
+- `Linked issue #123`
+- `pull request #45`
+- `PR #45`
+
+The helper should return sorted unique numbers.
+`MainWindow::issuesLinkedFromPull()` should combine helper results with `AgentSession::issueNumber` for local in-progress and recently completed agent sessions.
+`MainWindow::pullsLinkedToIssue()` should combine PR-side references with issue-thread PR references.
+
+## Agent Completion
+
+When `MainWindow::onAgentFinished()` successfully creates a PR for an issue session, it should store `session->prNumber` as it does today.
+Then it should post durable link notes for the issue and PR if they are missing.
+This should happen only after `PullStore::createPull()` returns a valid PR number.
+If one side of the link note fails to write, the agent log should record the error and the UI should keep the inferred link from `AgentSession`.
+The failure should not mark the successful agent run as failed because the code patch and PR creation already succeeded.
+
+For PR-conflict agent sessions with a linked issue, the replacement PR should also get the same explicit issue link.
+The original PR remains linked through its own existing references.
+The replacement PR should link to the issue if `session->issueNumber > 0`.
+
+## Data Flow
+
+Manual issue-page link:
+
+1. User clicks the issue sidebar link button.
+2. User chooses or types a PR number.
+3. ForkMesh posts the issue-side link comment if missing.
+4. ForkMesh posts the PR-side link comment if missing.
+5. ForkMesh reloads issues and PRs.
+6. ForkMesh re-renders the open issue or PR detail.
+
+Manual PR-page link:
+
+1. User clicks `Link issue`.
+2. User chooses or types an issue number.
+3. ForkMesh posts the PR-side link comment if missing.
+4. ForkMesh posts the issue-side link comment if missing.
+5. ForkMesh reloads issues and PRs.
+6. ForkMesh re-renders the open PR or issue detail.
+
+Agent issue completion:
+
+1. Agent succeeds and writes a patch.
+2. ForkMesh creates the PR.
+3. ForkMesh records `session->prNumber`.
+4. ForkMesh posts missing reciprocal link comments.
+5. ForkMesh reloads PRs.
+6. ForkMesh refreshes the issue list and re-renders the selected issue if it is still open.
+
+## Error Handling
+
+If a repo is read-only, manual link comments should continue to use the existing relay inbox fallback.
+If a relay submission fails asynchronously, the current implementation should at least delete the network reply and avoid blocking the UI.
+If a direct local comment write fails, log the failure with the issue or PR number.
+If the agent-created PR link comments fail, keep the PR and session because the primary agent work succeeded.
+If a typed issue or PR number does not exist locally, allow the note because mirrored or remote history may arrive later.
+
+## Testing
+
+Add unit coverage for the shared extraction helper.
+Verify issue references are extracted from PR titles, descriptions, branches, and comments.
+Verify PR references are extracted from issue comments.
+Verify duplicate references are de-duplicated and sorted.
+Verify manual link notes are recognized by the extraction helper.
+Add a focused store-level test for reciprocal link comments if it can be done without constructing `MainWindow`.
+Add a narrow regression test around `AgentSession::prNumber` plus PR description or link note recognition.
+Run `cd qt_client && ./run.sh test`.
+
+## Acceptance Criteria
+
+An agent-created PR appears in the issue `Development` section after the agent completes.
+The issue thread records a visible link note for the agent-created PR.
+The PR thread records a visible link note for the issue.
+Manual linking from the issue page still links both directions.
+Manual linking from the PR page still links both directions.
+Repeated linking does not create duplicate link comments.
+Existing closing keywords still drive merge-time issue closure.
+Existing explicit `Linked issue #N` and `Linked pull request #N` notes still work.
+The Qt test suite passes.
+
+## Open Decisions
+
+Use ordinary signed comments for the first implementation.
+This avoids changing canonical issue or PR event formats.
+
+Keep the current compact sidebar UI.
+This issue should make the Development section reliable, not build a full relationship management surface.
-- 
